# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
register_gate "tests/test_lock_timeout.py" "LOCK-TIMEOUT GATE: PASS" "every advisory-lock site arms lock_timeout before the blocking lock (audit r5)" "LOCK-TIMEOUT: every per-(account,repo) advisory-lock site must arm lock_timeout + statement_timeout BEFORE the blocking pg_advisory_lock, so no site can wedge forever on a contended/severed holder. The audited gap (two agents converged): only the live processor set them; the OFF-worker sites (co-change populate pool, boot self-heal reconcile, install/uninstall fan-out) took the blocking lock with NEITHER -- the unbounded-wait + leaked-connection class the live path was hardened against. Fix moves the arming INTO server_dbops._take_repo_lock (the single source of truth for the lock), so every site is guarded by construction. Proven (no DB, a recording cursor): _take_repo_lock issues SET lock_timeout AND SET statement_timeout BEFORE pg_advisory_lock, both to a POSITIVE bound (never 0/unlimited)" "every advisory-lock site arms lock_timeout + statement_timeout before the blocking lock, both positive (single source of truth in _take_repo_lock)" 20
